  "title": "Unusual Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "6587fe6a-b6f7-42e0-99fd-c5b78c62d215",
      "question": "Using 2025 as the baseline, which 10 sessions from January 2 through March 12, 2026 were the most unusual among the 50 most liquid US stocks, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T04:42:27.552309Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T04:43:17.207809Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Most unusual sessions (Jan 2 – Mar 12 2026) among the 50 most‑liquid U.S. stocks**\n*(baseline = all of 2025; anomaly scores are robust z‑scores, not forecasts)*\n\n| Rank | Date (UTC) | Ticker | Anomaly score | Features driving the anomaly (robust z‑score) |\n|------|------------|--------|--------------|----------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | 2026‑02‑25 | **CRCL** | 4.57 | **adj‑return 1d** +21.71 · **realized vol 20d** +8.05 · **adj‑return 5d** +7.49 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +5.02 |\n| 2 | 2026‑02‑06 | **CRWV** | 2.70 | **adj‑return 1d** +12.41 · **realized vol 20d** +5.96 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +0.82 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑1.08 |\n| 3 | 2026‑02‑06 | **BMNR** | 2.59 | **adj‑return 1d** +10.79 · **realized vol 20d** +5.44 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +2.20 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑4.68 |\n| 4 | 2026‑02‑13 | **COIN** | 1.58 | **adj‑return 1d** +10.26 · **realized vol 20d** +4.93 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +2.74 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑0.25 |\n| 5 | 2026‑02‑06 | **COIN** | 1.42 | **adj‑return 1d** +8.28 · **realized vol 20d** +3.42 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +1.80 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑3.74 |\n| 6 | 2026‑02‑06 | **CRCL** | 1.41 | **adj‑return 1d** +8.49 · **realized vol 20d** +3.71 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +1.34 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑2.75 |\n| 7 | 2026‑02‑09 | **APP**  | 1.41 | **adj‑return 1d** +8.40 · **realized vol 20d** +5.61 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +1.36 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑1.17 |\n| 8 | 2026‑01‑27 | **UNH**  | 1.36 | **adj‑return 1d** ‑12.28 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +7.71 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑4.10 · **realized vol 20d** +2.99 |\n| 9 | 2026‑01‑02 | **BMNR** | 1.26 | **adj‑return 1d** +9.29 · **realized vol 20d** +5.20 · **adj‑return 5d** +1.32 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +1.25 |\n|10| 2026‑02‑12 | **APP**  | 1.23 | **adj‑return 1d** ‑12.86 · **realized vol 20d** +6.71 · **log‑vol dev 20d** +2.94 · **adj‑return 5d** ‑0.43 |\n\n*All four monitored features (1‑day adjusted return, 5‑day adjusted return, 20‑day realized volatility, 20‑day log‑volume deviation) contributed; the largest absolute z‑scores are shown in bold.*\n\n**How the scan works**\n- Training window: 2025‑01‑01 → 2025‑12‑31 (11 230 observations).\n- Scoring window: 2026‑01‑02 → 2026‑03‑12 (2 400 observations).\n- The model flags sessions whose joint feature pattern deviates most from the 2025 baseline; the “anomaly_score” is a robust z‑score, not a probability or forecast[1].\n\n**Limitations**\n- Anomaly scores describe unusual observed feature combinations; they do not explain *why* a move occurred nor predict future moves.\n- Deviations are z‑scores against the 2025 baseline, not raw returns or percentages.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:b0a37773058058832aac792b56ad7332f75c01049d22f382bd465a390d706b50`",
